{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793650422,"nonce":"RJTUOeNNzCMMVgOwI1Q8+mq+7LI=","title":"Markdown renderer takes its colours from the layout stylesheet","message":"`MarkdownConfig` (crates/blinc_layout/src/markdown/config.rs) resolves eight colours from `ThemeState` when the config is built: `text_color`, `text_secondary`, `link_color`, `code_bg`, `code_text`, `blockquote_border`, `blockquote_bg`, `hr_color`. Both constructors read the theme once, and the renderer passes them inline to the widgets it builds, so rendered markdown keeps the scheme it was built under and the `.blinc-*` rules added in 950a86b never apply to it (the renderer passes `Some(config.blockquote_border)` etc. as overrides).\n\nFollow the pattern of 950a86b:\n- make the colour fields `Option\u003cColor\u003e`, `None` by default; set ones stay inline overrides;\n- let blockquote, hr, link, list and table take their `.blinc-*` rules when unset;\n- give the markdown root a class (`blinc-markdown`) with `color: var(--text-primary)`, and inline code and code blocks classes for `code_bg` / `code_text`;\n- body text spans: transparent when no colour is configured, so styled text inherits (styled text honours inherited CSS colour as of 110e0c03).\n\nCheck: a headless test rendering markdown in both schemes, as layout_widget_rules.rs does for the widgets; the markdown demo and the book's markdown page.","files":null}]}